% The tick form (tick/kitchen.llp) of ../kitchen_shared.llp: the second cook acts at its own pace (no turn of
% this cook's), so its load lines up with any of this cook's actions. Sibling card of kitchen_host.llp: the same kitchen with a second cook
% working the same pot. The explanation a wrong-domain surprise needs
% (an onion arrives in the pot that this cook never loaded) — a domain
% card, not a pack: its rule produces the kitchen's own atoms.
catalog kitchen_shared 1.
provenance text "a shared kitchen: a second cook also loads onions into the pot" "2026-10-11".
include "kitchen.llp".
weight w_partner.
stage task {
  %% the second cook drops an onion into the first cook's pot.
  %% target: kitchen
  partner_load [task] : pot_space -o pot_onion  @w w_partner.
}
#init hand_free 1
#query served
#query cooking
#query held_soup
#steps 12
